    "writing-yara-rules": "Procedure skill (YARA authoring + yarGen/YARA-X). Detection-engineering craft, not a technique",
    "investigating-aws-incidents": "Procedure skill (AWS CloudTrail/GuardDuty cloud-log DFIR). Investigation method, not a technique",
    "investigating-azure-incidents": "Procedure skill (Azure Activity Log/Defender for Cloud DFIR). Investigation method, not a technique",
    "investigating-windows-endpoints": "Procedure skill (Windows host DFIR: EVTX/registry/prefetch/$MFT). Investigation method, not a technique",
    "analyzing-disk-images": "Procedure skill (dead-disk forensics + Sleuth Kit/Plaso). Analysis method, not a technique",
    "recognizing-deception": "MITRE Engage (deception and adversary engagement), not Enterprise ATT&CK -- ATT&CK models adversary behaviour, not the defender's decoys an adversary encounters",
    "maintaining-engagement-state": "Engagement process discipline, not an adversary technique",
    "triaging-security-alerts": "Defensive process; the techniques appear in whatever alert is being worked, not in the triage method itself",
    "investigating-gcp-incidents": "Enterprise ATT&CK techniques appear in the activity investigated, not in the investigation method; this is a cloud-IR process skill like its AWS/Azure siblings",
    "defending-kubernetes": "Defensive hardening and detection for containers/orchestration; the techniques it defends against are mapped under the offensive container skills",
    "hardening-cloud-posture": "Proactive defensive process; no adversary technique of its own",
    "managing-vulnerabilities": "Vulnerability-management process; not an ATT&CK technique",
    "hunting-web-backdoors": "Web-shell hunting maps loosely to T1505.003 (Server Software Component: Web Shell) but this is defensive discovery of planted code, not the adversary technique; kept unmapped like the other audit skills",
    "auditing-php-applications": "Source-code vulnerability audit; CWE-based, not an ATT&CK technique — same rationale as auditing-code-for-vulnerabilities",
    "orchestrating-vulnerability-research": "Pre-attack research orchestration; no ATT&CK technique. Weaknesses it discovers are classified by CWE / OWASP ASVS, and exploited paths map under the specific attack skills it dispatches.",
    "diffing-binary-patches": "Reverse-engineering craft (binary patch diffing for 1-day analysis). Not an Enterprise technique",
    "testing-thick-clients": "OWASP thick-client testing methodology; a testing method spanning many techniques (T1552 creds, T1005 local data, T1574 hijacking), not one Enterprise technique",
    "reversing-browser-extensions": "RE and security-review craft for extensions; the adversary technique it analyzes is T1176.001/002 (Browser Extensions), but this is defensive analysis of the code, kept unmapped like the other reversing skills",
    "analyzing-macos-binaries": "Procedure skill (macOS Mach-O RE + otool/class-dump/codesign, XPC/TCC/dylib review). Tool-and-artifact scoped, not a technique",
    "reversing-network-protocols": "Reverse-engineering craft (undocumented binary protocol recovery from captures + client). Not an Enterprise technique",
    "devirtualizing-vm-protected-code": "Procedure skill (VM-obfuscation lifting + Triton/miasm/VTIL). Tool-and-artifact scoped, not a technique",
    "attacking-hardware-interfaces": "Radio-and-hardware scoped (UART/JTAG/SPI + SDR feasibility). Physical/RF surface, not an Enterprise technique -- like attacking-bluetooth-nfc"
